### Run it locally

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ cfg.public_repo }}.git && cd {{ cfg.public_repo.split('/')[1] }}
uv sync
uv run pytest
uv run jobpipe fixtures-build --dir data/fixtures
uv run jobpipe site --duckdb data/fixtures/warehouse.duckdb --public data/fixtures/public --out site
```

`jobpipe fixtures-build` runs the full dbt project on synthetic data, offline. A live run (`uv run jobpipe run`) needs network access and a `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `contents: write`, because state is stored in Release assets. `jobpipe backfill --from A --to B` replays stored snapshots, and `jobpipe rebuild` rebuilds the warehouse from every snapshot.

### Tests and CI

`ruff`, `mypy --strict`, `pytest` (unit tests, golden fixtures from 5 real boards, end-to-end runs against a fake GitHub API), a dbt build with {{ dbt_tests }} data tests on synthetic data, `pip-audit`, `gitleaks`, an internal link check, a 50 MB file guard and a commit-message check. Workflows: [ci.yml](.github/workflows/ci.yml), [daily.yml](.github/workflows/daily.yml), [checks.yml](.github/workflows/checks.yml).

